sam_docs: Heads-up — I'm putting together an SDK consumer error-behavior matrix (429s, timeouts, context-limit fallback, and graceful degradation). Need owners for per-SDK snippets + a short migration note for v2->v3 retry header changes. Can anyone pair on this?

maria_dev: I can own JS/TS snippets. Will include explicit try/catch + exponential backoff examples.

leo_engineer: I'll document runtime differences (hosted vs Dedicated) and capture a couple of logs showing 429 vs 503 behavior.

anya_se: Important: include which headers to expect (Retry-After, x-rate-limit-reset, x-request-id) and recommended SDK behaviors (respect Retry-After, parse HTTP-date vs seconds). Also call out fallback model chains.

sam_docs: Plan: create a docs page 'sdk-error-matrix' (internal slug), add per-sdk snippet files, and open a PR with a README + example runbook. I'll draft the PR by EOD. Who can run snippet smoke tests?

maria_dev: I'll add snippets for `@redwood/sdk` usage and raw fetch examples. Example snippet I'll include in the doc: 
```js
try {
  const res = await redwood.generate({ model: 'redwood-medium', input: prompt });
} catch (err) {
  if (err.status === 429) {
    // parse Retry-After and backoff
    const wait = parseRetryAfter(err.headers['retry-after']);
    await sleep(wait * 1000);
    // retry logic or fallthrough to smaller model
  }
  throw err;
}
```

leo_engineer: FYI: dedicated pools tend to return 503 on scaling events; hosted more often returns 429s when token windows or concurrency bubble. I'll attach two sanitized log snippets to the PR. Also add note about A/B fallback to a quantized model when latency matters.

anya_se: Add a short section on context trimming strategies (prompt chunking, summary + chain of thought truncation) and show sample config knobs: `max_tokens`, `context_window`, `nucleus_sampling` recommendation.

sam_docs: Linking to the internal runbook for reference: <https://redwood.internal/runbooks/errors#error-matrix>. We should also add a migration note for SDK v2->v3: `retry_header` changed shape and some clients must parse `x-retry-after-ms` fallback.

maria_dev: I'll add the migration section and include a unit test snippet that asserts `Retry-After` parsing handles both numeric and HTTP-date forms.

leo_engineer: Ran a quick experiment: sometimes Retry-After is an HTTP-date, sometimes seconds. We should include a `parseRetryAfter()` helper in our snippets.

docs_bot: Reminder: docs CI will lint the snippets; avoid >120 char lines and run `yarn docs:lint` locally before pushing.

sam_docs: Task list: @maria_dev -> JS/TS snippets + migration note, @leo_engineer -> runtime notes + logs + parse helper, @anya_se -> headers + fallback chain writeup, sam_docs -> PR + integrate into runbook + smoke runs. ETA tomorrow morning? :clock1: 

anya_se: ETA works for me. I'll drop the header sample logs here when ready.

maria_dev: Also including an example fallback config YAML to show model fallthrough order and timeout budgets: 
```yaml
fallback_chain:
  - model: redwood-large-quant
    timeout_ms: 1200
  - model: redwood-medium
    timeout_ms: 800
  - use_cache: true
```

sam_docs: Perfect. I'll create the draft page and open the PR, then ping for reviews. Thanks all! :tada:
